      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Yeah, it really feels like the bias for the mipmap could be calibrated to be sharper at your average viewing distance. If the previous solution was to turn off Mip-maps, I now understand why it was like that.\n\nIt's exceptionally blurry in comparison to the VRC+ Icon/Profile Picture  displayed right next to it. The examples in this Canny don't really show the contrast between the two. But it's easy to see in person.\n\nIt's also still inconsistently aligned. It just occurred to me that the mip-map issue is related to the inconsistent alignment. The alignment/scaling of the banner gets weird in a way that almost feels screen space like. Why does it need to do that? The icons don't do that.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-02-19T08:40:45.520Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Now that mipmapping for groups is a thing, they seem very aggressive. Even when someone isn't that far away, it is very soft and the details are lost. User icons don't seem to be affected as much.\n\nFor example, my WIndows 98 group, if the user is more than a couple of feet away, you can hardly tell there's text. And the group for the Great Pug has a nice half-tone pattern as a background which completely disappears.",
